1
00:00:00,160 --> 00:00:03,076
Sometimes we need to complain.

2
00:00:03,076 --> 00:00:06,080
But how can we do this politely

3
00:00:06,080 --> 00:00:08,160
and in a British way?

4
00:00:08,160 --> 00:00:11,200
First, we can begin 'would like to'

5
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:13,040
to say what we want.

6
00:00:13,040 --> 00:00:15,440
'Hi i would like to speak to the manager.

7
00:00:15,440 --> 00:00:17,280
Yes, I'd like to complain.'

8
00:00:17,280 --> 00:00:20,560
We can say 'I am unhappy about'

9
00:00:20,560 --> 00:00:22,825
plus a noun phrase.

10
00:00:22,825 --> 00:00:26,240
'Yes, I am unhappy about my late delivery.'

11
00:00:26,240 --> 00:00:29,280
We can also add 'very' or 'really'

12
00:00:29,280 --> 00:00:31,200
to make this stronger.

13
00:00:31,200 --> 00:00:34,080
'Yeah, I'm really unhappy about this.'

14
00:00:34,080 --> 00:00:37,440
We can also say 'it's unacceptable that'

15
00:00:37,440 --> 00:00:38,800
plus a clause.

16
00:00:38,800 --> 00:00:42,800
'Yeah, it's unacceptable\h
that my delivery is late.'

17
00:00:42,800 --> 00:00:45,680
Remember, don't lose your temper.

18
00:00:45,680 --> 00:00:49,120
This means 'don't become too angry' -

19
00:00:49,120 --> 00:00:51,520
it's rude to lose your temper.

20
00:00:51,520 --> 00:00:53,280
This is good advice -

21
00:00:53,280 --> 00:00:56,480
we can say this to people who are angry with us:

22
00:00:56,480 --> 00:01:01,840
'Alright! Don't lose your temper.'

